On Sun, 17 Aug 2014, Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> WRT Ludios, I'm not sure whether the displayed level number is where
> the Ludios portal is created or where it would be created *if* Ludios
> will be generated in case it's actually not guaranteed, but it would
> at least narrow down to the actual level where you have to look for it.

Nope.  The Ludios algorithm is a one-thirds chance on each vault between
level 10 and Medusa before it appears, with the Quest entry exempt.  The
only relevant information the game decides in advance is the depth of
Medusa.

It would be hard for the game to commit to a specific Ludios entry level,
because it's not known until the last minute whether a given level will
even have a vault.

The number you see on ^O is probably just the depth of Ludios' single
level.  No level number is shown to the player, but one is still needed
internally for things like deciding what difficulty of monsters to spawn.

